# PayAlert — local configuration template
#
# PayAlert needs NO credentials to build or run. Detection, transaction history, the
# cashbook, reminders, the payment QR, export and backup all work entirely on-device,
# with no account. There is also no monetization of any kind.
#
# Optional team pairing uses Google sign-in and Supabase pairing metadata only.
# No payment data is uploaded. Neither Gradle nor the app reads dotenv files.
#
# Never commit real credentials. `.env` is git-ignored.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: Android team pairing (public configuration, embedded in the APK)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Export these variables before running Gradle, supply matching
# -PSUPABASE_URL=... and -PSUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=... project properties, or put
# them in the git-ignored root `secrets.properties` file for persistent local builds.
# Project properties take precedence, then environment variables, then that local file.
# Both default to empty: pairing is then unconfigured and performs no network requests.
# HTTPS origins only (no URL paths).
# Use an sb_publishable_ key or legacy anon JWT, NEVER service_role/sb_secret_ keys.
# Invalid/private keys are rejected during the build, before embedding any value.
# Enable Google in Supabase Auth, and allow this exact redirect URL:
# com.vivekray898.payalert://auth/callback
# The app opens the external browser and handles the callback automatically.
# Signing out attempts to revoke the current auth session
# and clears local auth; it does not delete server pairings or local payment data.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: build overrides
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APP_DISPLAY_NAME=PayAlert
